Version 4
SHEET 1 1280 900
TEXT 72 48 Left 3 ;TP2 Simulation 3 - stable oscillator, block-level equivalent
TEXT 72 96 Left 2 ;This schematic models the second switched-capacitor oscillator at block level with two ideal integrators.
TEXT 72 136 Left 2 ;Run, then plot V(X), V(Y), and V(KICK). Target output frequency is 20 Hz.
TEXT 72 192 Left 2 !.param fe=1000
TEXT 72 232 Left 2 !.param f0=20
TEXT 72 272 Left 2 !.param k=2*sin(pi*f0/fe)
TEXT 72 312 Left 2 !.param C2=10p
TEXT 72 352 Left 2 !.param C1={k*C2}
TEXT 72 392 Left 2 !.param omega=2*pi*f0
TEXT 72 452 Left 2 ;Equivalent continuous-time block model: dx/dt = omega*y + startup pulse, dy/dt = -omega*x.
TEXT 72 512 Left 2 !CX X 0 1 IC=0
TEXT 72 552 Left 2 !CY Y 0 1 IC=0
TEXT 72 592 Left 2 !BX 0 X I={omega*V(Y)}
TEXT 72 632 Left 2 !BY 0 Y I={-omega*V(X)}
TEXT 72 692 Left 2 ;Startup pulse, analogous to the pulse source requested in the TP to initiate oscillation.
TEXT 72 732 Left 2 !VKICK KICK 0 PULSE(0 1 100m 1u 1u 1m 10)
TEXT 72 772 Left 2 !IKICK 0 X PULSE(0 1000 100m 1u 1u 1m 10)
TEXT 640 192 Left 2 ;For the real switched-capacitor implementation at 20 Hz:
TEXT 640 232 Left 2 ;k = 2*sin(pi*20/1000) = 0.1256
TEXT 640 272 Left 2 ;C2 = 10 pF, so C1 = k*C2 = 1.26 pF
TEXT 640 332 Left 2 ;The pulse is needed because with exactly zero initial conditions an ideal oscillator remains at rest.
TEXT 640 360 Left 2 ;IKICK injects a 1 ms current pulse into the X integrator capacitor, giving x an initial displacement.
TEXT 640 392 Left 2 !.tran 0 2 0 100u uic
TEXT 640 432 Left 2 !.options method=gear reltol=0.003
